   "id": 530196,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2dc0f516144c3b95.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Li Yu, et al./BMC Evolutionary Biology)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>One of the phylogenetic trees proposed for bears (family Ursidae) is shown in the image.</p>\n<p>What are the two oldest species in this family according to this tree?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1037272,
     "content_html": "The brown bear (grizzly) and the polar bear."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037273,
     "content_html": "The Asian and American black bears."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037274,
     "content_html": "The sun ber and the sloth bear."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037275,
     "content_html": "The spectacled bear and the giant pands."
    }
   ],
